      "content": "Beyond yellowing leaves due to nitrogen deficiency, you can look for extended dieback of leaves, dark green foliage as nitrogen becomes excessive, or growths of anthracnose fungus, possibly indicating disrupted microbial life. Soil physicality also matters; compacted soil, slow drainage, or an unpleasant smell could signal imbalance. Lastly, maintaining organic matter content, avoiding over-tilling, and practicing crop rotation are all beneficial for robust soil microbes. Proactive observation and regular soil assessments will guide your adjustments to support microbial health while addressing nutrient deficiencies.",
